{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/508454-do-you-bring-anything-from-wta-to-wtf","id":508454,"title":"Do you bring anything from WtA to WtF?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-05-08T15:01:50-07:00","id":508454,"title":"Do you bring anything from WtA to WtF?","content":"Now, I know that the obvious supposition is that there's absolutely no contact between fandoms when it comes Werewolf: The Apocalypse and Werewolf: The Forsaken, but let's just call me an optimist.<br /> <br /> If there are any fans of WtA who made the jump to WtF, for whatever reason, did you bring anything over with you? Do you tweak your Forsaken setting in some ways to homage, reference, or just outright bring-in elements of (or shout-outs to) WtA?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5487-voiddrifter","name":"VoidDrifter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-08T17:03:07-07:00","id":508558,"title":"","content":"I haven't run game in 2e; I've been toying with making a few of the WtA lodges or very small tribes - I don't think I'd be able to make all of them work. Right now I'm thinking of the Fianna as a lodge who have taken the Fey and Hedge critters as their sacred prey","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/324-ardenty","name":"ardenty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar324_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-08T17:27:08-07:00","id":508569,"title":"","content":"I guess Pentex, though I had to cut out a lot of stuff that was over the top or didn't make sense in the new world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-08T17:47:32-07:00","id":508574,"title":"","content":"Other than treating the Forsaken/Pure conflict like a lesser War of Rage no, I don't bring anything over because the one thing I would have brought was already ported over (the Maeljin). Continuing that line of thought, Banes can be represented with Wound tainted spirits. Apocalypse is great if you want splatterpunk style horror, I like the comparatively subdued feel Forsaken has a bit more. I also prefer the local focus of Forsaken to the Umbra traveling of Apocalypse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-08T18:25:18-07:00","id":508605,"title":"","content":"I do love the Cosmology, interconnected world, and main Antagonists, but I'd hesitate to borrow major structural elements from W:tA for Forsaken.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-08T20:09:40-07:00","id":508656,"title":"","content":"I'd use the tribes as lodges, they are always available in my games. Metis are out, wolf born are in (but they were in anyway via rumors and nighthorrors) albeit at a substantial fluke (i.e. .00001% chance of occurring). Not sure how i'd handle the black spirals beyond as a lodge, though probably all as bale hounds. I love both worlds, but I think i'd leave em both mostly intact.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-09T05:17:17-07:00","id":508867,"title":"","content":"Was wanting to start a thread like this, only I need the 2ed Lodges framework for that. Will hurry the devs on this. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> And I would totally see Black Spilars as very prominent Bale Hounds Lodge also. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-09T14:39:32-07:00","id":509247,"title":"","content":"Interesting to see people here. I'm still &quot;getting into&quot; Apocalypse material, but, whilst I admit a preference for Forsaken (especially Forsaken 2e), there's some things I'm interested in bringing over. So far, one or two of the Other Breeds might make good for alternative shapeshifting breeds (using Skinchangers and War Against The Pure as my guide; I refuse to acknowledge Changing Breeds), and like others have noted here, some of the Apocalypse tribes might make good Forsaken lodges.<br /> <br /> Also, Pentex might be interesting to bring over as a &quot;Big Bad&quot; that almost any species could lock horns with, if I could just figure out how...<br /> <br /> Something I've done is make Lupus (wolf-born wolves) a thing in my homebrewed setting, with some changing:<br /> * Werewolves and wolves are infertile together, unless the werewolf is already a Lupus or until a werewolf has reached a minimum Primal Urge of 4.<br /> * The &quot;species&quot; of the children of such a pairing depends on the mother; wolf pups are born if the mother is a wolf, or a werewolf that remains in wolf/near-wolf/primal wolf (is that still a thing?) form through the pregnancy, whilst a female werewolf who returns to human or.near-human form for the pregnancy gives birth to human children.<br /> * Humans born of a wolf/werewolf pregnancy are always wolf-blooded, and much more prone to manifesting shapeshifting-based Tells.<br /> * A litter of wolf pups born from such a union will contain only one, or rarely two, Lupus.<br /> * All Lupus require a direct werewolf/wolf pairing to occur; &quot;wolf-blooded wolves&quot; don't exist.There are rumors that non-Lupus werewolf pups and their descendants are touched by the spirits in some way, such as requiring a lower Primal Urge for a werewolf to breed with them.<br /> * Lupus exist as ordinary wolves until they make their First Change.<br /> * Lupus are vastly more common amongst the Pure (who A: hold more of the woodland territories, B: are anti-humanists as a rule, and C: regard Lupus werewolves as purer or sacred somehow) than they are amongst the Forsaken.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5487-voiddrifter","name":"VoidDrifter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-09T15:24:27-07:00","id":509269,"title":"","content":"Primal Form is not a thing in WtF 2e, no. Though I did make a homebrew version of it as an alternative to Father's Form.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-10T01:30:08-07:00","id":509731,"title":"","content":"What <i>would</i> you call forsaken wolf-kinfolk anyway? You can't call them &quot;wolf-blooded&quot;. That would just be silly. Man-blooded? Hmm.<br /> <br /> Is there a gender-neutral one-syllable word for human?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-10T06:38:31-07:00","id":509826,"title":"","content":"I think wolf blooded still works as its spiritual not physical (not purely anyway).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-10T06:45:44-07:00","id":509830,"title":"","content":"I guess you'd never hear them complain if you called them that. Most of them can't talk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-10T10:43:29-07:00","id":510005,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/508454-do-you-bring-anything-from-wta-to-wtf?p=509731#post509731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What <i>would</i> you call forsaken wolf-kinfolk anyway? You can't call them &quot;wolf-blooded&quot;. That would just be silly. Man-blooded? Hmm.<br /> <br /> Is there a gender-neutral one-syllable word for human?</div> </div> </div> </div>Technically the &quot;were&quot; prefix in the term werewolf is a gender-specific term for adult male humans, so there's prescedent for Uratha culture using gendered terminology. <br /> <br /> Though, I think what I would do is put in a request for a First Tongue translation of &quot;Human-Blooded&quot; and use that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-10T10:59:13-07:00","id":510010,"title":"","content":"Do we have even a first tongue word for <i>wolf</i> blooded?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-10T11:21:26-07:00","id":510058,"title":"","content":"We have a name for Wolf (Spirits) Borthers - Uralath - I spopose &quot;Ur-&quot; part means &quot;wolf&quot; in First Tounge, seeing it in Uratha term and in Firstborns names.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-10T11:25:58-07:00","id":510063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/508454-do-you-bring-anything-from-wta-to-wtf?p=510010#post510010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do we have even a first tongue word for <i>wolf</i> blooded?</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Uragarum.</i> There's also <i>Urdurgarum, </i>which literally means Wolf-Blooded child and could either be used to refer to a child who is wolf-blooded, or the child of a wolf-blooded. <i>Ur-Kahrih</i> is wolf-suckled, and refers to Wolf-Blooded with the Raised by Wolves Merit. <i>Ursumugarum</i> is literally wolf-children-blooded and refers to the child of two werewolves.<br /> <br /> I'm pretty sure all of the above is non-canon, but accurate to de-grimmified Sumerian, so it pretty much checks out. There's also <i>Urazakh-Angir</i> from Night Horrors: Wolfsbane, whose name meant Wolf-Born-Foretold. I assume the <i>Angir</i> part is the &quot;foretold&quot;, so if you wanted to include lupine Wolf-Blooded and didn't want the name to sound silly I personally would go with <i> Urazakh,</i> or Wolf-Born.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-10T11:35:39-07:00","id":510070,"title":"","content":"<i>Blood of the Wolf</i> calls them <i>uragarum</i>. So perhaps not all non-canon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-10T11:42:57-07:00","id":510072,"title":"","content":"I came up with all the terms except <i>uragarum</i>; they come from my dictionary. <i>Urazakh</i> would be good for the wolfborn wolfblooded. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> There's also <i>lu'uragarum</i>, which I came up with for a scrapped story/concept idea \u2014 it means &quot;[that which] houses the manwolf&quot;, and plays on the meaning of <i>uragarum</i>, which itself means &quot;[that which] houses the wolf&quot;.<br /> <br /> As for the original point of the thread: I have borrowed spirits and totems from W:tA for my stuff. I converted a couple of W:tA totems into 1e Forsaken totems, but I never posted them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-14T14:37:41-07:00","id":514492,"title":"","content":"While I'm not a W:tA guy, I was inspired by an idea someone else had regarding importing Pentex somewhere on the forum. The idea was that Pentex could serve a similar role to the one it does in W:tA, cooperating with or enslaving spirits in order to more agressively market their products and exploit people. Unlike the original idea, I'd probably have their spirit bosses not be the Maejin, but instead have it be Guhinim Thirih\u2019Lulul, an Idigam given a brief mention in the 2e core.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-14T18:25:23-07:00","id":514687,"title":"","content":"I want to bring back WtA Tribes as Lodges in 2ed WtF, but we still do not have Lodges rules... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-15T09:02:59-07:00","id":515238,"title":"","content":"The conversion guide has that. And it's the fluff there that matters","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-15T14:45:20-07:00","id":515453,"title":"","content":"I've brought over the First Ronin as a reminder of what happens when you break Harmony against the pack.<br /> Nightmaster as one of the earliest Bale Hounds who lives within wounds.<br /> Stargazers as a lodge of the Blood Talons who use meditation and martial arts as a way to focus the rage into something more defined.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1250-shadowlost","name":"Shadowlost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1250_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"155"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-15T16:06:16-07:00","id":515518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/508454-do-you-bring-anything-from-wta-to-wtf?p=515238#post515238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The conversion guide has that. And it's the fluff there that matters</div> </div> </div> </div>Up untill you gone to benfits section. &quot;Harmony mdifiers&quot; are most of the time useless, as 2ED use very diffrent mechanics for this trait and it's definition. Renown are also buyed in other ways. As the Gifts also. So mechanical part of &quot;WtA Tribes as Lodges&quot; need to be rewriten for WTF 2ED.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}